menu "Witness Wi-Fi OTA and log download"

    config WITNESS_WIFI_SSID_OVERRIDE
        string "Fixed access point SSID (empty = witness-XXXX from the MAC)"
        default ""
        help
            The default SSID is "witness-" plus the last two bytes of the
            chip's MAC address. Set this to use a fixed name instead, for
            example when the eFuse MAC cannot be read reliably.

    config WITNESS_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Access point WPA2 password (8..63 characters)"
        default "witness-ota-2026"
        help
            Anyone with this password can upload firmware while Wi-Fi is on
            (Pad Idle or Landed only). Change it for your own build.

    config WITNESS_WIFI_CHANNEL
        int "Access point channel"
        range 1 13
        default 6

    config WITNESS_WIFI_TX_POWER_DBM
        int "Default Wi-Fi maximum TX power (dBm)"
        range 2 20
        default 8
        help
            Applied with esp_wifi_set_max_tx_power (0.25 dBm units). The Wi-Fi
            enable command can override it for one session.

    config WITNESS_WIFI_AUTO_OFF_MINUTES
        int "Default Wi-Fi auto-off time without HTTP activity (minutes)"
        range 1 240
        default 15

    config WITNESS_WIFI_CONFIRM_MINUTES
        int "Wi-Fi window after an OTA update's first boot (minutes, 0 = none)"
        range 0 240
        default 5
        help
            The one exception to "Wi-Fi never starts at boot": the first boot of
            a freshly uploaded image (pending verification), once its self-test
            passes and the image is marked valid, opens the access point for
            this long so the host can confirm the new version over HTTP. It is
            skipped outside Pad Idle/Landed. 0 disables it; the host then has
            to send the Wi-Fi on command again.

endmenu
